    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-38049",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf",
      "knowledge_point": "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial",
      "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+8x+2 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8{x}^{2}-30x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8{x}^{2}-32x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x-8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8}{x-4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+8x+2 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8{x}^{2}-30x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8{x}^{2}-32x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x-8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8$ by the linear binomial $x-4$ gives\n\n- the quotient $6{x}^{2}+8x+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder $0.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8}{x-4}=6{x}^{2}+8x+2+\\frac{0}{x-4}=6{x}^{2}+8x+2.\n$$",
